# Review package: batch 2, slice install

## fa5e1090 Stop the app before the database copy, remove the services a build does not name, and take over an update an old updater began

An old updater can hand an update to the new build's own. A restart in the middle goes on from where it stood, the time limit ends the installer's whole process group, and a failed update rolls back.

Ruling: a restart at step backup starts the stopped app first; a restart during the second copy stays on the hand-over path; the time limit kills the installer's whole group; 'This build's updater goes on with the update.' goes to status.json before applied - why: each is needed for the update's promise, tested, and judged sound by review - cost if wrong: one more dump or a slower restart.

